    {
      "file": "sections/method.tex",
      "before": "The comparative cohort covers non-neutral matches in 1980--2024; earlier eligible records initialize strength.",
      "after": "The comparative cohort covers non-neutral matches in 1980--2024; earlier eligible records initialize strength. This boundary separates historical initialization from the principal comparisons; it is a study-scope choice, not evidence that earlier matches are uninformative.",
      "reason": "补清1980边界含义，不虚构早期比赛无价值或最佳截点。"
    },
    {
      "file": "sections/method.tex",
      "before": "The estimated positive slope $b$ maps strength to the probability scale; integrating over the distribution avoids treating estimated strength as known.",
      "after": "The estimated positive slope $b$ maps strength to the probability scale; integrating over the distribution avoids treating estimated strength as known. Its positivity preserves the ordering of predicted home-win probability with respect to the mean strength difference when context and uncertainty are fixed.",
      "reason": "补正斜率的实际数学作用；固定其他条件时单调，不声称不确定性不同仍全序。"
    },
    {
      "file": "sections/method.tex",
      "before": "Lower scores indicate better probability forecasts~\\cite{gneiting2007scoring}.",
      "after": "Lower scores indicate better probability forecasts~\\cite{gneiting2007scoring}. Logarithms are natural, and the loss is averaged per match.",
      "reason": "说明对数底数与平均单位，便于复现解释。"
    },
    {
      "file": "sections/method.tex",
      "before": "The prospective central 90\\% ranges propagate latent strength uncertainty with coefficients fixed, excluding coefficient and model error.",
      "after": "The prospective central 90\\% ranges propagate latent strength uncertainty with coefficients fixed, excluding coefficient and model error. They describe uncertainty about a predicted probability, rather than a range of possible match results or a guarantee of forecast accuracy.",
      "reason": "明确概率区间与结果不确定性/准确率保证的区别。"
    },
    {
      "file": "sections/results.tex",
      "before": "The largest loss difference was between context-only and strength-only prediction",
      "after": "The largest loss difference was between background-only and strength-only prediction",
      "reason": "与表和图统一对照模型名称。"
    },
    {
      "file": "sections/results.tex",
      "before": "Adding context also reduced the Brier score from $0.193698$ to $0.192657$ and mean bias from $+0.9308$ to $+0.2398$~pp.",
      "after": "Adding context also reduced the Brier score from $0.193698$ to $0.192657$ and mean bias from $+0.9308$ to $+0.2398$~pp. These changes concern probability quality; the corresponding classification improvement is small because accuracy depends only on which side of the decision threshold a prediction falls.",
